WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.760
Wanna know what Pinhead looks like underneath all&nbsp;
those pins? We've got such sights to show you.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.740
It was only a matter of time until "Hellraiser"&nbsp;
got the reboot treatment. After all, there aren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.660
many classic horror IPs left that haven't&nbsp;
been reimagined for modern times. Arguably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.440
"Hellraiser" could benefit from a reboot&nbsp;
as the original franchise went off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.340
rails long before it had the chance to&nbsp;
realize its full potential. Instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.720
making the most of Clive Barker's unique&nbsp;
mythology, the sadistic saga churned out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.620
a series of underwhelming sequels that were&nbsp;
barely connected to the "Hellraiser" lore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.760
Who would have guessed this would refer&nbsp;
to the feeling of watching the sequels?

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:43.653
"Pain has a face. Allow me to show it to you."

00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:47.220
While it remains to be seen if the new&nbsp;
movie will spawn sequels that take the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.540
franchise to new heights, fans can rest&nbsp;
assured knowing Hulu's upcoming slice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:57.060
Cenobite-centric chaos has such sights to show&nbsp;
us. The filmmakers certainly aren't interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.460
in recreating Barker's 1987 original film, as&nbsp;
evidenced by the casting of Jamie Clayton as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.440
the terrifying sadomasochistic demon Pinhead.&nbsp;
The original Hell Priest was brought to life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:13.020
by Doug Bradley and his performances solidified&nbsp;
both him and the character as bona fide horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.460
icons. The new take on Pinhead is quite a&nbsp;
departure from Bradley's version, and early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.140
"Hellraiser" trailers suggest that Clayton has&nbsp;
made the role her own in the best way possible.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.940
Jamie Clayton is unrecognizable in the new&nbsp;
"Hellraiser." Boasting black eyes, pale skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.279
scarred flesh, and pins sticking out of&nbsp;
her head, she doesn't look human at all.

00:01:31.408 --> 00:01:35.640
However, the performer behind the pins&nbsp;
and grotesque demonic makeup is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.680
gorgeous in real life. Television aficionados&nbsp;
will know her from shows such as "Sense8,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.780
which saw her play an LGBTQ hacktivist&nbsp;
and political blogger named Nomi Marks.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.700
Elsewhere, Clayton is known for her performance&nbsp;
as Sasha Booker on "Designated Survivor" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.860
Tess Van De Berg on "The L Word: Generation Q."&nbsp;
But now that she's had the opportunity to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.880
a horror icon, Pinhead might be the role&nbsp;
she's most synonymous with moving forward.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.260
In many ways, Jamie Clayton's Pinhead is&nbsp;
a throwback to the original Hell Priest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.340
In Clive Barker's novella "The Hellbound&nbsp;
Heart," which the original "Hellraiser"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.300
is adapted from, the cenobites are&nbsp;
often described in androgynous terms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.388
so making this version of Pinhead a&nbsp;
little less masculine makes perfect sense.

00:02:16.388 --> 00:02:20.880
However, David Bruckner has also promised&nbsp;
fans that Clayton's Pinhead will be unlike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.540
any previous iteration of the character.&nbsp;
While speaking to Entertainment Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.700
the "Hellraiser" director confirmed that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.260
Pinhead is a complete reimagining and&nbsp;
praised Clayton's performance. He said,

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:34.740
"We knew we wanted Pinhead to be&nbsp;
a woman. Jamie was just the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.060
person for the role. A person's identity can&nbsp;
be really exciting for a role in many ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.260
but I have to emphasize that Jamie&nbsp;
absolutely killed, that's how we got there."

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.700
Additionally, Bruckner wasn't interested in&nbsp;
having Clayton copy Doug Bradley's Pinhead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.780
as the English actor has already perfected&nbsp;
that iteration of the character. He added,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.820
"We didn't want to do a Doug Bradley impression,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.660
we just didn't think that's possible to do.&nbsp;
There will be suffering, but you're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:02.000
get a sense of what Pinhead's desires might&nbsp;
be in a way that hits a little different."

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.820
Pinhead will be appearing in your nightmares&nbsp;
when "Hellraiser" drops on Hulu next month.

